From fe294c9dde2da39a6df820052ea08285f1c02e84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:47:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 216/219] fix: take the BVH walk out of ConeTracePS' pass loop
 and make fMultTriRT fold

The engine's own HLSL compiler could not build Total_Illumination@ConeTracePS(X1):
"internal error: compilation aborted unexpectedly". The harness had reported the
permutation clean because its failure test grepped for ": error", which fxc does
not print for an internal error - both compilers (Windows SDK 10.0.26100.7705 and
the engine's C:/Windows/System32/d3dcompiler_47.dll, 10.0.26100.9444) fail on it
in exactly the same way, so the compiler binary was never the difference.

Cause, from a git bisect of the RT branch with the engine compiler: ConeTracePS
built cleanly up to 122bb991 (dynamic meshes) and started failing at 7d884755
(full material reconstruction at the hit). The triangle tracer and the voxel cone
tracer were sharing one instantiation of ConeTraceTree - the call passed the
runtime value "bUseRT ? 1 : 0" for fMultTriRT, so RT_TraverseTris and
RT_ProcessBestHit had to be generated inside the cone body as well. On top of
that the 2026-09-13 loop peel (const int p = 0; if (p == 0)) had only hidden the
earlier X3511 "forced to unroll loop, but unrolling failed" behind the internal
error.

Structural change:

* ConeTracePS: the stock "for (int p = 0; p < nPassesNum; p++)" is the only loop
  header again - the hand peel is gone. The call inside it passes the LITERAL 0
  for fMultTriRT, i.e. exactly the text the native path preprocesses to, so the
  loop body fxc unrolls is the stock cone trace and nothing else. An RT pixel
  breaks out on the loop's first line and gets ONE ConeTraceTreeAndSky call with
  the LITERAL 1 after the loop, followed by the whole post-trace contract it
  needs: bRTWriteGData, the debug views, the NO_TESSELLATION multiply and the
  ALD/RGB write that doubles as the incomplete-traversal fallback. The in-loop
  RT special cases (mirror kernel, portal bending opt-out, ray length, origin
  offset, RT_ResetInfo) moved into that block; the loop body is stock again.

* ConeTraceTree: fMultTriRT is const. ConeTraceBrick takes it inout (it zeroes
  the multiplier past VOX_MAX_RT_DIST_RAY so the voxels stop shrinking) and one
  write from an inlined callee turns the constant into a phi, after which nothing
  folds. The RT gates now read the const parameter and ConeTraceBrick gets a
  mutable copy of its own.

The native path is unchanged: without %_RT_QUALITY every added line preprocesses
away and the call site is character for character CE 5.7.1's.

This is not yet the whole fix. With both compilers the three ConeTracePS entries
that carry the engine's real specular flag set still hit the same internal error:
the triangle tracer plus RT_ProcessBestHit's material reconstruction is over
fxc's capacity for this entry point by less than the blend-layer block of
decision 10 (removing either half of that block compiles). See
scene-notes/rt/reports/06a-unroll-fix.md for the measurements and the options.

